# CLAUDE.md — {{ cluster_name }}

Guidance for Claude Code (claude.ai/code) working in this repository.

**Read [`.claude/skills/cluster-development/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/cluster-development/SKILL.md)
before making any change here.** It carries the non-negotiable workflow, the
invariants that break production when violated, the change-type decision tree
and the pre-merge gates, and it points at every canonical document. This file
exists so that an agent which opens `CLAUDE.md` first still lands there.

Nothing from the skill is repeated here: a second copy of the rules is a second
copy to keep current, and the skill is the one the tooling loads.

## Template first

This repository is one cluster, not the product. Site data — inventory values,
addresses, the application estate, this cluster's documents — stays here.
Anything generic goes upstream first: a role, a CI job template, a Terraform
module or a shared gate to weisssrv-lib, and a repository-shape change to
weisssrv-cluster-template. It then arrives here as a `lib_ref` bump or a
`copier update`. The skill's § Where the generic half of a change goes is the
table; `README.md` § Reference names every document this repository owns.
